---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | InfraOpsX"
  description="About InfraOpsX — practical infrastructure engineering focused on Linux, Docker, Kubernetes, storage, networking and production troubleshooting."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  enPath="/about/"
  zhPath="/zh/about/"
>
  <Header locale="en" switchHref="/zh/about/" />

  <main>
    <section class="showcase-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label">ABOUT INFRAOPSX</span>
        <h1>Infrastructure work grounded in real systems.</h1>

        <p>
          InfraOpsX focuses on practical infrastructure engineering:
          deploying services, diagnosing failures and keeping systems
          understandable after the work is finished.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="showcase-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="showcase-grid">
          <article class="showcase-card">
            <span class="showcase-kicker">What I work with</span>
            <h2>Linux, containers and production infrastructure</h2>

            <p>
              My work covers Linux servers, Docker and Docker Compose,
              Kubernetes, Nginx, networking, storage, Prometheus, Grafana
              and the systems around them.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="showcase-card">
            <span class="showcase-kicker">How I approach problems</span>
            <h2>Diagnose before changing things</h2>

            <p>
              Infrastructure failures rarely exist in isolation. I prefer to
              start with logs, metrics, system state and actual constraints,
              then make the smallest change that safely solves the problem.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="showcase-card">
            <span class="showcase-kicker">Why this site exists</span>
            <h2>Real incidents become useful technical notes</h2>

            <p>
              InfraOpsX documents practical troubleshooting and deployment
              work. Sensitive details are removed, but the technical reasoning,
              commands and lessons are kept useful for people facing similar
              problems.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="showcase-card">
            <span class="showcase-kicker">Working together</span>
            <h2>Clear context leads to better solutions</h2>

            <p>
              If you need help with a deployment, migration or infrastructure
              problem, include the environment, symptoms, relevant logs and
              what has already been tried.
            </p>

            <div class="portfolio-links">
              <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact InfraOpsX</a>
              <a class="button secondary" href="/case-studies/">Case Studies</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer locale="en" />
</BaseLayout>
